        },
        {
          "_id": "pgSession1000001",
          "name": "Session 1",
          "type": "text",
          "sort": 100,
          "ownership": { "default": -1 },
          "text": {
            "format": 1,
            "content": "<p>SESSION-ONE-TEXT: the party met in the tavern and took the job from the miller, who paid in old coin and told them about the road north, the well at the crossing, the bridge that floods every spring, and the smith who has not left his forge in a year. They argued about the price, slept badly, and set out before dawn with two days of food and one lantern between them. On the road they met a pedlar who sold them a map he swore was true, and a dog that followed them for a mile and then turned back as if it knew better.</p>"
          }
        }
      ]
